{"t": 51.063, "n": 44, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "The plan now names SIL-AC10 in two test rows, so it no longer goes unnamed. I haven't run any tests or checks.\n\nSIL-AC10 is the criterion of SIL-B19. This task edits SIL-B19, but no test file carried the id. Its three clauses are that a refused payload is redelivered, that a daily cap skips the judges, and that a dry run files nothing.\n\nI changed these parts of `plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i170c.plan.md` and nothing else:\n- **Row 3.4** (`tests/test_filing.py`) is changed: its comment now names SIL-AC10. It covers the redelivery and dry-run clauses, and it now also serves R3. Its Completed mark is emptied.\n- **Row 3.8** is new (`tests/test_autonomy.py`, kind `test`, serves R3). It adds SIL-AC10 to the comment on `test_daily_cap_skips_the_judges_and_records`, which covers the daily-cap clause. Only that comment changes, and the row's Completed cell is empty.\n- **R3** lists SIL-AC10 among its spec ids.\n- **Section 0** has a bullet recording this trip back and the extra files I opened: lines 165–185 and 212 of `self-improvement.spec.md`, lines 185–216 of `test_filing.py`, and lines 70–100 of `test_autonomy.py`.\n- **Status** is back to `planned`, since two rows are unmarked.\n\nAll other rows keep their marks. Complexity stays `complex`. The proof table is unchanged, because it has one row per criterion of the task and SIL-AC10 isn't one of them.\n\nI did not run git; the engine commits the plan.\n\nARTIFACT plan: plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i170c.plan.md\nARTIFACT complexity: complex", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "c4413ddd-1ee0-4402-b1dc-e13224325ea1"}
